From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Tue, 01 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman: port: quiet spurious WARN_ON in O/H fifo-size verification (phase 1c polish)

Board-tested 2026-09-01 on .185 (image vyos-2026.09.01-1756-rolling,
commit 4fa5d70c): "bringup 4" succeeded (fman_port_config()+
fman_port_init() both returned 0, expected "oh_test bringup 0x04 OK"
logged) -- 0178's fix worked. But dmesg also showed a WARN_ON splat
from fman_port_init()+0x230, inside verify_size_of_fifo().

Root cause: verify_size_of_fifo() is unmodified upstream mainline --
it only ever handled FMAN_PORT_TYPE_TX and FMAN_PORT_TYPE_RX via an
if/else-if chain, with both size sums initialized to 0 and never
otherwise touched for any other type. For O/H, neither branch matches,
so min_fifo_size_required stays 0 and WARN_ON(min_fifo_size_required
<= 0) fires on every call. This has no functional consequence --
port->fifo_bufs.num is never negative, so the two dev_dbg comparisons
just below were already a silent no-op for O/H either way -- but it's
a noisy, spurious warning that would fire on every future bring-up,
and is worth fixing properly rather than leaving in place.

Fix: O/H now takes the TX branch, not a new one. Justified because
O/H is architecturally closer to TX here, not RX: FMBM_OFDNE and
FMBM_TFDNE both use NIA_ENG_QMI_DEQ (see init_bmi_oh(), 0176) --
both are QMI-dequeue-driven, unlike RX which receives directly from
the wire. Every field the TX formula reads is already populated
generically for O/H: max_frame_length (DFLT_PORT_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH,
set unconditionally in fman_port_config()) and
cfg->tx_fifo_deq_pipeline_depth (BMI_DEQUEUE_PIPELINE_DEPTH(), set
unconditionally in set_dflt_cfg() for every port type). port_speed
is simply 0 for O/H, which only selects which back-to-back margin
constant applies, not correctness.

Not yet re-tested on hardware after this fix (queued for the next
board session, alongside re-confirming "bringup 4" is now
warning-free).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: A (adds one type to an existing TX-only branch condition; RX path and every other type untouched)
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
index 3142258cc..868a4fe0b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
@@ -1038,8 +1038,24 @@ static int verify_size_of_fifo(struct fman_port *port)
 {
 	u32 min_fifo_size_required = 0, opt_fifo_size_for_b2b = 0;

-	/* TX Ports */
-	if (port->port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_TX) {
+	/*
+	 * TX Ports. ASK2 OH-port re-enqueue infra (dpaa1) also takes this
+	 * branch, not RX's. Board-tested 2026-09-01 on .185: this upstream
+	 * function only ever handled TX/RX, so both sums stayed 0 for O/H,
+	 * tripping the WARN_ON below on every bringup call. Harmless --
+	 * fifo_bufs.num is never negative, so the dev_dbg verification a
+	 * few lines down was a silent no-op either way -- but noisy, and
+	 * worth fixing properly since O/H is architecturally closer to TX
+	 * here. Both are QMI-dequeue-driven: FMBM_OFDNE and FMBM_TFDNE both
+	 * use NIA_ENG_QMI_DEQ, see init_bmi_oh(). Every field this formula
+	 * reads is already populated generically for O/H: max_frame_length
+	 * and cfg->tx_fifo_deq_pipeline_depth by set_dflt_cfg() for every
+	 * port type, unconditionally; port_speed is simply 0 for O/H, which
+	 * only changes which b2b-margin constant applies below, not
+	 * correctness.
+	 */
+	if (port->port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_TX ||
+	    port->port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_OH) {
 		min_fifo_size_required = (u32)
 		    (roundup(port->max_frame_length,
 			     FMAN_BMI_FIFO_UNITS) + (3 * FMAN_BMI_FIFO_UNITS));
